# ============================================================
# STANDING OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS — REQUIRED IN EVERY PHASE
# ============================================================

The human investigator must be able to copy/paste the entire important result set out of Databricks as plain text.

DO NOT leave an important result only in:
- a Databricks `display()` table,
- a results grid,
- a chart,
- an interactive widget,
- or a persisted table without printing its contents.

For EVERY clinically important analysis, print a concise plain-text version directly in notebook output.

Preferred formats:

### Small tables
Print as Markdown or plain text with all rows.

### Medium tables
Use something equivalent to:
`pandas_df.to_string(index=False)`

or Spark:
`df.show(n=<enough rows>, truncate=False)`

Do NOT truncate important columns.

### Large patient-level tables
Do NOT print thousands of rows.

Instead print:
- total row count
- unique patient count
- schema
- summary counts
- important distributions
- first 20 rows
- 20 random rows using a fixed seed
- all edge/discordant cases up to a reasonable maximum
- persisted table name

