Do this BEFORE calculating any downstream statistic.

# ============================================================
# NEVER USE STALE DENOMINATORS
# ============================================================

Every summary statistic must be generated directly from the dataframe being analyzed in that cell.

Do NOT manually type or reuse an old N.

Do NOT use hard-coded cohort counts.

For example, never write:

`n = 144`

because an earlier version contained 144 patients.

Instead calculate:

`n = current_df.select("pat").distinct().count()`

or the equivalent.

Project-level tables must be generated programmatically from the FINAL canonical cohorts.

# ============================================================
# EXPLICIT UNIT LABELING
# ============================================================

Every number must indicate whether it represents:

- PATIENTS
- TREATMENT LINES
- DRUG EPISODES
- ADMINISTRATIONS
- PROCEDURES
- IMAGING STUDIES
- LAB RESULTS
- ENCOUNTERS
