# ============================================================
# SANITY / CLINICAL PLAUSIBILITY CHECK
# ============================================================

After every major result ask:

"Would this number make clinical sense at Johns Hopkins?"

Examples of mandatory red flags:

- nearly every patient hospitalized on treatment day 0
- only 20% of HCC patients having AFP
- hundreds of "first-line" treatments before approval
- more systemic patients than exist in the systemic cohort
- ALBI missing in a cohort despite >90% availability elsewhere
- ALBI grade being treated as Child-Pugh class
- essentially zero surgeries despite hundreds of hepatectomy codes
- a procedure code being assigned a clinical indication without corroboration
- a large change in N without an attrition waterfall

When a result is surprising:

DO NOT rationalize it automatically.

Instead print:

`CLINICAL PLAUSIBILITY ALERT`

and investigate:
1. denominator
2. unit
3. source mapping
4. code meaning
5. join keys
6. date window
7. duplicate rows
8. missing synonyms
9. left truncation
10. competing indication

