# ============================================================
# IMPORTANT BEHAVIORAL RULE
# ============================================================

Execution success does NOT mean scientific validation.

"All cells executed" is not a completion criterion.

A phase is complete only when:

- counts reconcile,
- units are explicit,
- invariants pass,
- unexpected findings are investigated,
- important outputs are printed,
- persisted tables read back correctly,
- and unresolved ambiguities are clearly labeled.

Never give a project recommendation from internally inconsistent data.
